{"id": "122792", "revid": "144844", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=122792", "title": "Cachoeiro de Itapemirim", "text": "Cachoeira de Itapemirim is a city of 211,000 people (2020) in southern Esp\u00edrito Santo.\nUnderstand.\nThere are great geological attractions such as Frade e a Freira, Pico do Itabira, Pedra da Ema and Pico da Pedra da Penha, the highest point in the municipality from where you can see the Atlantic Ocean. It is possible to reach its summit in the middle of the forest, which has a chapel of Nossa Senhora da Penha and a cross, in its vicinity there is the Cachoeira Alta.\nGet in.\nCachoeiro de Itapemirim Airport,\u00a0known as Raimundo de Andrade Airport, offers short flights.\nThe municipality has access via the BR-101, ES-482, ES-393, ES-489, ES-482 and ES-166 highways.\nGet around.\nThe municipality has an integrated urban transport system carried out by Cons\u00f3rcio Novo Trans.\u00a0Urban public transport is provided by Flecha Branca (including the Gruta district), district public transport is provided by Via\u00e7\u00e3o Costa Sul (Soturno, Gironda and C\u00f3rrego dos Monos), Via\u00e7\u00e3o Santa Luzia (Itaoca, Coutinho\u00a0and\u00a0S\u00e3o Vicente) and Via\u00e7\u00e3o Real (Burarama, Pacotuba, Conduru).\u00a0All public transport has the same design, with the urban and district ones distinguished by the color blue and green, respectively."}
