{"id": "122794", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=122794", "title": "Colatina", "text": "Colatina is in the Northwest of Esp\u00edrito Santo state in Brazil. It lies on the banks of the Doce river. Its population was 123,400 in 2020.\nUnderstand.\nIt offers great potential for ecotourism, as there are beautiful landscapes and well-kept farms in the countryside.\u00a0Highlight for S\u00e3o Pedro Frio, at 600 meters of altitude, 40 km from the Center, which offers visitors a mountain climate.\u00a0It is worth visiting the lakes of Lim\u00e3o, Pau Gigante, Coroa Verde, Barbados, Oil, Patr\u00e3o Mor.\u00a0In addition to the Oito, Onze, Vinte and On\u00e7a waterfalls.\nEvery afternoon, when the sun approaches the mountainous horizon, the sky and the bed of the\u00a0Rio Doce\u00a0merge in gold and red and make up a magnificent sunset.\u00a0The famous sunset of the city, which is known as Princesa do Norte, represents the postcard, along with the monument of Christ the Redeemer, which is 33 meters high, located in the upper part of the municipality, in the Bela Vista neighborhood.\u00a0\nGet in.\n127\u00a0km north of the capital\u00a0Vit\u00f3ria\u00a0and on the trainline from\u00a0Vit\u00f3ria\u00a0to\u00a0Minas Gerais. "}
