{"id": "123088", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=123088", "title": "Schwabenheim", "text": "Schwabenheim an der Selz is a small village in Rhenish Hesse in the state Rhineland-Palatinate of Germany.\nUnderstand.\nSet in the Selz valley this village is surrounded by the vineyards of Rhenish Hesse \"(Rheinhessen)\". A nice rural area but nothing in particular for the tourist except an above average number of excellent restaurants.\nGet in.\nSouth from Ingelheim on the L428.\nBuy.\nGood priced wines direct from the wineries."}
