{"id": "123133", "revid": "1423298", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=123133", "title": "Bombinhas", "text": "Bombinhas is in the Itaja\u00ed Valley region of Santa Catarina.\u00a0Its clear and unpolluted waters attracts tourists from all over the world\u00a0to its beaches suitable for all kinds of water sports and preserved vegetation.\nUnderstand.\nBombinhas is a peninsula, almost an island, which juts 12 kilometers into the sea, including 22 beaches and four islands.\nBombinhas is part of the surroundings of the Marine Biological Reserve of Arvoredo, which has an area of \u200b\u200b17,800 hectares formed by the islands of Arvoredo, Gal\u00e9s and Deserta.\nThe first beach entering the municipality is Bombas, good for surfing, diving, fishing and walks on the trails of Parque da Galheta.\u00a0Bombinhas beach, with its calm waters and white sand, is an invitation for pleasant hours with the family and for swimming and diving.\u00a0Retiro dos Padres is an almost private beach where tranquility reigns, with waves that are almost always calm and a history of rescue of English shipwrecked by the local population that gave rise to the name Praia dos Ingleses.\u00a0Praia de 4 Ilhas (known among the natives as Praia de Fora) is nationally known for its strong waves, ideal for surfing.\u00a0Praia de Mariscal is an extensive beach with great waves for surfing and certainly one of the best preserved in the state.\u00a0Canto Grande beach has a narrow strip of land that separates a beach with calm waters and an unforgettable sunset from one with special waves for surfing.\u00a0The bay of Zimbros is contagious for the peace and tranquility only broken by the noise of the engines of the fishing boats.\u00a0Tainha beach is the most isolated with a privileged natural beauty.\nGet in.\nBy plane.\nNavegantes airport\u00a0is\u00a0the closest to Bombinhas, at a distance of about 47 km.\u00a0Another alternative is\u00a0Florian\u00f3polis airport, about 70 km away.\nBy bus.\nThe municipality does not have a bus terminal.\nThe companies that operate are:\nAs timetables and lines are very limited, it may be necessary to travel to the\u00a0Balne\u00e1rio Cambori\u00fa\u00a0Bus Terminal (Balne\u00e1rio Cambori\u00fa Bus Terminal - TRBC, about 30 km from Bombinhas) or\u00a0Itaja\u00ed\u00a0(Itaja\u00ed International Bus Terminal - Terri, about 42 km from Bombinhas).\nGet around.\nIt has a municipal transport system (without terminals), operated by\u00a0Via\u00e7\u00e3o Praiana Ltda.\u00a0"}
