{"id": "123146", "revid": "144844", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=123146", "title": "Rio Bonito", "text": "Rio Bonito is a municipality of the region of Grande Niter\u00f3i, in the metropolitan area of Rio de Janeiro, in the Rio de Janeiro state.\nUnderstand.\nRio Bonito is a peripheral, partially rural municipality belonging to the metropolitan agglomeration of Rio de Janeiro. It has a relatively small population, and has wide areas of environmental protection (just like several other municipalities located on the outskirts of the Rio's metro area). Rio Bonito is the easternmost municipality in the Greater Rio region, and it was in the downtown area of this municipality that the urban expansion of the metropolitan agglomeration of Rio de Janeiro along the vector of the BR-101 highway ended.\nGet in.\nIn the city center of Rio de Janeiro, there are urban bus and van lines to Rio Bonito. Bus lines to Rio Bonito depart from Terminal Menezes C\u00f4rtes, in Castelo, and from the region of Candel\u00e1ria - both in Rio city center. The van line to Rio Bonito departs from the Central do Brasil surrounding area.\nThe main road access to Rio Bonito for those coming from Rio downtown area is the BR-101 highway (Rio-Vit\u00f3ria highway)."}
