{"id": "123200", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=123200", "title": "Jaguar\u00e3o", "text": "Jaguar\u00e3o is a city in the Southeast of Rio Grande do Sul, on the border with Uruguay.\nGet in.\nBR-116 from Pelotas and Porto Alegre to the north.\nIntercity buses stop at the at the corner of Pra\u00e7a Comendador Azevedo. Buses are available from Porto Alegre.\nTo get in from R\u00edo Branco, across the border in Uruguay, just cross the, which does not have border controls. You're free to cross back and forth between the two cities, but if you're coming from Uruguay and want to continue farther into Brazil, or if you're coming from Brazil and want to continue farther into Uruguay, you're required to go through passport controls in both cities, which to make things more confusing and difficult are located some distance away from the border on each side. is located several blocks into Jaguar\u00e3o at Rua J\u00falio de Castilhos 1572, and is on the outskirts of R\u00edo Branco at the end of Bulevar Aparicio Saravia."}
