{"id": "123254", "revid": "1423298", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=123254", "title": "Correia Pinto", "text": "Correia Pinto is a town of 15,000 people (2010) in the Serrana of Santa Catarina.\nUnderstand.\nThe main industry in the town is pulp and paper.\nGet in.\nCorreia Pinto is 225 km from Florian\u00f3polis.\nDo.\nIts main festive dates take place in May (Festa do Pe\u00e3o La\u00e7ador) and September (Farroupilha Week)."}
{"id": "123255", "revid": "1423298", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=123255", "title": "Santa Cec\u00edlia (Santa Catarina)", "text": "Santa Cec\u00edlia is in the Serrana of Santa Catarina.\nUnderstand.\nSanta Cec\u00edlia is a small town, culturally influenced by the rural ways of the farm, by the mountain caboclo, coming from the mixture of the Indian with the tropeiros and European immigrants.\u00a0The people carry traces of the tropeira culture, with influences from S\u00e3o Paulo and Rio Grande do Sul.\u00a0\nIt sits on the Santa Catarina plateau, with vast pine forests, in the middle of Serra Geral, being one of the municipalities with the coldest climate in all of Brazil.\nSee.\nThe city has some tourist and historical attractions:"}
